# grammar spec projection — GAP-134 item 5
#
# WHAT THIS IS. `docs/spec/grammar.md` is the one remaining hand-written
# grammar document and the artifact this gap's title names. This generator
# replaces the hand-maintained FACT TABLES in it with tables projected from
# the one executable grammar-fact owner, `lib/compiler/token.id` (read
# through its generated bridge `src/grammar_role_table.zig`, exactly the way
# `gate/treesitter/agreement.id` reads the owner). Nothing here invents a
# production: every row is a fact the owner already publishes.
#
# WHAT STAYS AUTHORED. The document's prose (law citations, delimiter
# rulings, the closed lexical law) is not generated. A projection formats
# facts; it does not write law. The generated region is delimited by two
# markers, the same shape `scripts/treesitter_emit.id` established for
# ext/tree-sitter-idol/grammar.js, so regeneration is byte-checkable.
#
# THE CHECK: `idol check scripts/grammar/spec.id && sh gate/grammar/spec.sh`
# The gate regenerates privately and fails unless the tracked markdown is
# byte-identical; a damaged owner fact must CHANGE the projection (positive
# control), and a generator that cannot run exits 3 rather than agreeing.
#
# WHY A SHELL-FREE .id GENERATOR ON THIS HOST: `idol run` refuses DNB004 on
# this Linux box (no direct native realization), so an Idol-body generator
# cannot execute here. The route that DOES execute is reading the owner's
# generated Zig bridge and formatting it — the same route
# `gate/treesitter/agreement.id` uses. This file keeps the Idol front for
# when DNB004 lifts; the shell gate below drives the actual projection today
# and both are named in gaps/GAP-134.md.

path = "docs/spec/grammar.md"
begin = "<!-- grammar:begin -->"
end = "<!-- grammar:end -->"
